{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-11_16-25-56-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\np='update-stage12.json'\nd=json.load(open(p))\nd['sources'] = [\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"s_pipeline_replicate\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"replication.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":446,\\\"end_line\\\":510,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"s_pipeline_send\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"replication.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":512,\\\"end_line\\\":532,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"s_pipeline_decode\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"replication.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":534,\\\"end_line\\\":567,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"s_set_previous_log\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"replication.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":587,\\\"end_line\\\":612,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"s_update_last_appended\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"replication.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":655,\\\"end_line\\\":665,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n]\nd['investigations'].append({\n \\\"ref\\\":\\\"@pipeline-next-index-progress\\\",\n \\\"question\\\":\\\"Can pipelined replication leave the leader's per-follower nextIndex ahead of what the follower has acknowledged, or stall progress, given that the pipeline advances its own send cursor before any response arrives?\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"s_pipeline_replicate\\\",\\\"s_pipeline_send\\\",\\\"s_pipeline_decode\\\",\\\"s_update_last_appended\\\",\\\"s_set_previous_log\\\"],\n \\\"hypothesis\\\":\\\"pipelineSend advances a pipeline-local next index to last entry index + 1 immediately after handing the request to the pipeline, while the per-follower nextIndex and the commitment map are only updated from decoded responses in pipelineDecode via updateLastAppended. If the local cursor were also the acknowledged cursor, a dropped or rejected request could leave the leader believing the follower had entries it never stored, and a terminal failure could stall replication.\\\",\n \\\"discriminator\\\":\\\"Trace where the two cursors are updated and what happens on the first unsuccessful pipeline response or a setup error: a defect needs the acknowledged nextIndex (or commitment) to advance without a successful response, or replication to stop without falling back. If the local cursor is private to pipelineSend, s.nextIndex and commitment move only on successful decoded responses, the pipeline aborts on the first NACK and standard replication resumes from the acknowledged index, and setup errors route to the snapshot path, then the concern is refuted for this path.\\\",\n \\\"disposition\\\":\\\"explained\\\",\n \\\"limitations\\\":[\n   \\\"Source-only: no execution was requested, so this is a reading of cursor ownership and fallback rather than an observed pipeline failure.\\\",\n   \\\"The transport contract (InmemTransport and NetworkTransport pipelines deliver responses in order and close on error) was assumed, not exercised.\\\",\n   \\\"Behaviour of concurrent stop, removal and shutdown paths while a pipeline is in flight was not traced.\\\"\n ]\n})\nd['knowledge'].append({\n \\\"kind\\\":\\\"behavior\\\",\n \\\"statement\\\":\\\"Pipelined replication keeps two separate cursors: pipelineSend advances a private send cursor to the last pipelined entry index + 1 as soon as the request is handed to the pipeline, while the per-follower nextIndex and the commitment map advance only from successful decoded responses (updateLastAppended stores nextIndex = last entry index + 1 and matches commitment, then notifies the verify futures as leader). The decoder aborts the pipeline on the first unsuccessful response, on a newer term (notifyAll(false) plus a step-down notification) and pipelineSend returns shouldStop when setup fails such as a compacted prefix, after which the caller falls back to standard replication or the snapshot path. setPreviousLog additionally special-cases nextIndex-1 equal to the last snapshot index so a snapshot-backed prefix is accepted as the previous log entry.\\\",\n \\\"conditions\\\":\\\"Applies to the leader-side pipeline path in the captured revision for peers that support AppendEntriesPipeline, including the fallback to replicateTo after the pipeline aborts.\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"s_pipeline_replicate\\\",\\\"s_pipeline_send\\\",\\\"s_pipeline_decode\\\",\\\"s_update_last_appended\\\",\\\"s_set_previous_log\\\"]\n})\nd['interpretations'].append({\n \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"@pipeline-next-index-progress\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"s_pipeline_replicate\\\",\\\"s_pipeline_send\\\",\\\"s_pipeline_decode\\\",\\\"s_update_last_appended\\\",\\\"s_set_previous_log\\\"],\n \\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"explained\\\",\n \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The optimistic advance is confined to the pipeline and does not become acknowledged state. pipelineSend builds each request from the current local cursor (setupAppendEntries) and, only after the request is accepted by the pipeline, stores last.Index+1 into that private cursor (replication.go:512-532); the per-follower s.nextIndex and the commitment map are updated exclusively from successful decoded responses through updateLastAppended, which also notifies any waiting verify futures that the leader is still leader (replication.go:534-567, 655-665). Any unsuccessful response stops the decoder, which makes pipelineReplicate return and the replicate loop fall back to standard replication from the last acknowledged nextIndex, so a rejected batch cannot be treated as stored; a newer term additionally notifies the followers' votes as false and signals step-down, and a setup failure in pipelineSend returns shouldStop without sending, which sends the loop back through the standard path where a missing prefix becomes the snapshot path (replication.go:446-510, 224-296). setPreviousLog's snapshot case (replication.go:587-612) covers the boundary where the previous entry is exactly the snapshot index rather than a stored log. No defect is claimed from this reading: the cursor separation plus the abort-and-fall-back rule is an enclosing protection for the concern.\\\",\n \\\"counterevidence\\\":[\\\"The local cursor is only used to build the next pipelined request; nothing else reads it, so an in-flight NACK cannot promote unacknowledged entries into s.nextIndex or into commitment.\\\"],\n \\\"limitations\\\":[\\\"Source-only; no pipeline failure, out-of-order close or stop-while-in-flight execution was requested.\\\",\\\"Assumes the transport pipeline delivers responses in order and reports errors through the same path, which was read but not exercised.\\\"]\n})\njson.dump(d, open(p,'w'), indent=2)\nprint(sorted(d), [s['id'] for s in d['sources']], len(d['investigations']), len(d['knowledge']), len(d['interpretations']))\nPY\ncd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-11_16-25-56-hashicorp_raft-real-run && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-11_16-25-56-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update-stage12.json 2>&1 | tail -3; date -u\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
